{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/utgb2pcn","slideIndex":3,"position":{"left":84,"top":578,"width":700,"height":32},"text":"Configured reconstruction threshold: 0.037624","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":18,"typeface":"Aptos","color":"#A8BBC5","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/muy4r1","slideIndex":3,"text":"“Detection has two parts. The LSTM autoencoder measures reconstruction error across all three physical variables over the full 24-hour window, matching the scope of the configured threshold. Additional checks look at the final hours for flatlined humidity or temperature and sudden pressure jumps. A pressure drop paired with a humidity rise can be treated as a severe-weather pass. For recovery, a separate one-dimensional Kalman filter per variable smooths the signal and skips a flagged current measurement.”"}
