{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/8ekbgw","slideIndex":5,"text":"“The stack is deliberately straightforward. Python and FastAPI serve the inference endpoint; PyTorch runs the LSTM model; NumPy and scikit-learn prepare and scale features; Joblib loads the saved scaler. The front end is plain HTML, CSS, and JavaScript. Open-Meteo supplies city lookup and hourly weather estimates.”"}
